# .gitleaksignore — known-safe patterns that gitleaks should not flag.
# Each line is a SHA256 fingerprint of a finding that has been audited
# and confirmed safe. Generated format: gitleaks detect --report-format json
# then hash each finding's fingerprint field.
#
# CANARY SENTINELS (internal/canary/canary.go)
# These KEYLATCH_CANARY_* strings are intentional test sentinels embedded in
# the binary to detect credential leakage. They are not real secrets.
# They must live in internal/canary/ and nowhere else (enforced by CI).
#
# To add a new entry: run `gitleaks detect --report-format json -r /tmp/report.json`
# then for each false-positive finding, record its Fingerprint field here.
